Package: arimatools
Type: Package
Title: Teaching-Oriented Tools for Empirical ARIMA Modelling
Version: 0.3.2
Authors@R: person("Miguel A.", "Arranz", email = "maarranz@eco.uc3m.es",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5951-2284"))
Description: Tables, summaries, numerical forecasts and figures for empirical
    ARIMA modelling, developed for Applied Time Series Econometrics (ATSE) at
    Universidad Carlos III de Madrid. R port of the Python package ARIMA-Tools.
    Complements 'forecast' and 'stats' with root and common-root diagnostics,
    coefficient inference, residual diagnostics, dynamic effects, recursive
    parameter stability, transparent order searches, psi-weight forecast-error
    variances, fan charts, and outlier regressors, detection and effect plots.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    forecast (>= 8.21),
    ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0),
    patchwork,
    stats,
    utils,
    zoo
Suggests:
    plotly,
    lmtest,
    tsoutliers,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
